# FMG Catering — Core Rules

## Always

- Use reusable components and proper folder structure (`client/`, `server/`, `database/`)
- Validate all user inputs on client and server
- Protect admin/staff routes with JWT middleware and role guards
- Keep client-facing pages public (no login)
- Use meaningful variable names; write maintainable code
- Store credentials in environment variables (`.env`), never hardcode

## Never

- Use machine learning terminology or ML libraries
- Create customer login functionality
- Expose admin or staff routes without authentication
- Hardcode database credentials

## Terminology

- "Rule-based recommendations" / "decision support" — not AI or ML
- "Analytics" — predefined logic on historical data
- Roles: `public`, `staff`, `admin`

## UI Theme

- White background, gold accents (`#C9A227` or similar)
- Professional catering branding; responsive; accessible
